course: dictionary
lesson: 9205
title: Solar: to do with the Sun
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Solar is an adjective. It means to do with the Sun, or coming from the Sun. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it, because they are clues. «In a solar eclipse the Moon is between the Sun and the Earth.» The words Sun and Earth tell you that solar is linked to the Sun.
explain: The Solar System has capital letters because it is a name. It is the Sun and everything that goes around it: eight planets, moons, asteroids and comets. «The Solar System formed about 4.6 billion years ago.» So the Solar System is the Sun's family.
explain: Solar energy is energy from sunlight. Solar panels on roofs collect it. «Countries are switching to solar, wind and other clean energy.» Here solar is a kind of energy. Ask yourself: does the sentence still make sense if I put "from the Sun" in place of the word? If yes, you have the right meaning.
fact: Solar means to do with the Sun, or coming from the Sun.
fact: The Solar System is the Sun and everything that goes around it, including eight planets.
fact: Solar energy is energy from sunlight, collected by solar panels. It is renewable and clean.
fact: A solar eclipse happens when the Moon passes between the Earth and the Sun.
fact: Never look straight at the Sun, even during an eclipse.
exercise: What is the Solar System? | *The Sun and everything that goes around it | A group of shops in a town | Only the Earth and the Moon | A type of cold cloud
exercise: «Solar panels on the roof collect energy from the sunlight.» What do solar panels collect? | Heat from burning coal | *Energy from sunlight | Sound from the street | Rain water
exercise: «About 4.6 billion years ago there was no Sun and no Earth, only a huge, cold cloud of gas and dust called the solar nebula.» Find and copy the word that means to do with the Sun. | cloud | *solar | gas | billion
test: What does a solar eclipse happen when? | Jupiter passes the Moon | The Earth passes between the Sun and the Moon | *The Moon passes between the Earth and the Sun | The Sun goes out for a week
test: Why is solar energy called clean? | It makes lots of smoke | *It burns no fuel and gives off no carbon dioxide while it works | It comes from coal | It only works at night
exam: «Solar-powered calculators and garden lights work using light.» What do solar-powered calculators use to work? | Sound | *Light | Water | Wind
